    <!-- Activation Functions -->
    <section class="section" id="activation-functions">
      <span class="section-label">Core Concepts</span>
      <h2>Activation Functions: Introducing Nonlinearity</h2>
      <p>Activation functions transform neuron outputs, introducing nonlinearity that enables deep networks to learn complex patterns. Without activation functions, stacking layers would be equivalent to applying a single linear transformation—pointless.</p>

      <p><strong>ReLU (Rectified Linear Unit):</strong> f(x) = max(0, x). Simple, fast, and highly effective. Outputs zero for negative inputs, identity for positive inputs. Most widely used in modern deep learning.</p>

      <p><strong>Sigmoid:</strong> f(x) = 1 / (1 + e^-x). Squashes values to (0, 1), useful for binary classification output layers. Can suffer from vanishing gradients in deep networks.</p>

      <p><strong>Tanh:</strong> f(x) = (e^x - e^-x) / (e^x + e^-x). Similar to sigmoid but outputs (-1, 1). Zero-centered, often works better in hidden layers than sigmoid.</p>

      <p><strong>Softmax:</strong> Used in output layers for multi-class classification. Converts raw scores to probability distribution across classes.</p>

      <h3>Visualizing Activation Functions</h3>
      <div class="code-header"><span class="code-lang">Python</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div>
      <pre><code><span class="kw">import</span> <span class="im">numpy</span> <span class="kw">as</span> <span class="im">np</span>
<span class="kw">import</span> <span class="im">matplotlib</span>.<span class="im">pyplot</span> <span class="kw">as</span> <span class="im">plt</span>

<span class="cm"># Define activation functions</span>
<span class="va">x</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="bi">np</span>.<span class="fn">linspace</span>(<span class="nm">-5</span>, <span class="nm">5</span>, <span class="nm">100</span>)

<span class="cm"># ReLU</span>
<span class="va">relu</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="bi">np</span>.<span class="fn">maximum</span>(<span class="nm">0</span>, <span class="va">x</span>)

<span class="cm"># Sigmoid</span>
<span class="va">sigmoid</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="nm">1</span> <span class="op">/</span> (<span class="nm">1</span> <span class="op">+</span> <span class="bi">np</span>.<span class="fn">exp</span>(<span class="op">-</span><span class="va">x</span>))

<span class="cm"># Tanh</span>
<span class="va">tanh</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="bi">np</span>.<span class="fn">tanh</span>(<span class="va">x</span>)

<span class="cm"># Plot</span>
<span class="im">plt</span>.<span class="fn">plot</span>(<span class="va">x</span>, <span class="va">relu</span>, <span class="dt">label</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="st">'ReLU'</span>, <span class="dt">linewidth</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="nm">2</span>)
<span class="im">plt</span>.<span class="fn">plot</span>(<span class="va">x</span>, <span class="va">sigmoid</span>, <span class="dt">label</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="st">'Sigmoid'</span>, <span class="dt">linewidth</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="nm">2</span>)
<span class="im">plt</span>.<span class="fn">plot</span>(<span class="va">x</span>, <span class="va">tanh</span>, <span class="dt">label</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="st">'Tanh'</span>, <span class="dt">linewidth</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="nm">2</span>)
<span class="im">plt</span>.<span class="fn">legend</span>()
<span class="im">plt</span>.<span class="fn">xlabel</span>(<span class="st">'Input'</span>)
<span class="im">plt</span>.<span class="fn">ylabel</span>(<span class="st">'Output'</span>)
