    </section>

    <!-- Key Takeaways -->
    <section class="section" id="takeaways">
      <span class="section-label">Summary</span>
      <h2>Key Takeaways</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Neurons apply weighted sums and nonlinear activations</strong> — this composition across layers creates universal approximators</li>
        <li><strong>Activation functions are critical</strong> — they introduce nonlinearity; without them deep networks would be just linear models</li>
        <li><strong>Forward propagation computes outputs</strong> — data flows through layers, each transforming input to output</li>
        <li><strong>Backpropagation enables learning</strong> — it efficiently computes gradients through the chain rule, allowing weight updates</li>
        <li><strong>Deep networks learn hierarchically</strong> — early layers learn simple patterns, later layers combine them into complex representations</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

